    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-upside matchups today, headlined by the elite efficiency ratings of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.87) and **Kyle Tucker** (81.22). **Gunnar Henderson** is the day\u2019s standout, benefiting from a favorable wind-out environment and a high-leverage spot in the order against Roki Sasaki. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** (74.42) are primed for success against Trey Gibson; both players draw significant value from the soft 5.63 xERA of the opposing starter, combined with wind-out conditions that inflate their power profiles. **Josh Jung** (63.35) and **Nolan Schanuel** (62.53) also project as strong starts, with **Nolan Schanuel** finding a rare sweet spot by avoiding a platoon disadvantage while benefiting from a boost in a favorable park.\n\nThe decision to start **Jackson Merrill** (52.45) despite facing the formidable deGrom demonstrates our commitment to plate appearances over raw matchup ease, though the \"Elite Hold\" risk associated with deGrom limits his ceiling. On the bench, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.54) serves as our most difficult exclusion. While he possesses a robust base projection, he ultimately fell short of our starters because of his matchup against Be Brown, whose 3.48 xERA suppresses the overall efficiency score compared to the softer matchups exploited by **Coby Mayo** or **Brayan Rocchio**. We remain on high alert for official lineup confirmations for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**; any shift away from their projected top-six spots would trigger an immediate re-evaluation of their daily efficiency and potential benching to preserve game caps.",
